@host = http://localhost:5180

### Sign in as Fleet Manager (full access)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "manager@crewlink.dev", "password": "manager123" }

### Sign in as Crew Member (own records only)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "crew@crewlink.dev", "password": "crew123" }

@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### The fleet
GET {{host}}/api/vessels?pageSize=5&sort=name
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Vessel names only - readable by any signed-in user, unlike the register above
GET {{host}}/api/vessels/lookup
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Crew directory, filtered and searched server-side
GET {{host}}/api/crew?search=Santos&status=Onboard&pageSize=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Certificates expiring within 30 days - the band is a SQL range scan, not a per-row computation
GET {{host}}/api/certifications?bucket=Within 30 days&pageSize=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Dashboard KPIs and chart series
GET {{host}}/api/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Derived notifications
GET {{host}}/api/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Rule 2: expect 422 with the per-rank shortfall when the vessel is below manning
PATCH {{host}}/api/vessels/vessel-0001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "readyToSail": true }

### Validation: expect 400 with fieldErrors.imoNumber (check digit is wrong)
POST {{host}}/api/vessels
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "MV Bad Number",
  "imoNumber": "1234568",
  "flag": "Panama",
  "type": "Tanker",
  "status": "In Service",
  "minimumSafeManning": { "Master": 1, "AB": 4 },
  "readyToSail": false
}

### Rule 1: expect 422 listing the rotation that already covers those dates
POST {{host}}/api/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "crewId": "crew-demo-0001",
  "vesselId": "vessel-0001",
  "rankOnboard": "Chief Officer",
  "signOnDate": "2026-08-01",
  "signOffDate": "2026-10-01",
  "port": "Singapore",
  "status": "Planned"
}
